  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between [(3S,4aS)-5-acetyloxy-6,8,10-trihydroxy-1,1,4a-trimethyl-9-oxo-7-(2-propan-2-yloxypropyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-phenanthren-3-yl] acetate and PITSLRE serine/threonine-protein kinase CDC2L1, mediated through UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10. This compound is identified as a target of both acetamide and sennoside D, which are known to interact with CDC2L1. The shared target of these two compounds implies a potential mechanism of action involving the UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, which may facilitate the activation or inhibition of CDC2L1 through the metabolism of these agents. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of CDC2L1 via a pathway that involves the enzyme UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2B10, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
